{
 "id": "326-49",
 "split": "setup_long",
 "sentences": [
  "I want to emphasize the importance of clean and readable code.",
  "One of the ways we ensure that is by always using annotations for functions.",
  "It's a simple practice but it makes a big difference in maintaining high-quality code.",
  "I want you to get used to this practice from the start.",
  "Always annotate your functions, no matter how simple they may seem.",
  "It's a non-negotiable part of our coding standards.",
  "Now, I'll be reviewing your code regularly and providing you with feedback.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about our practices.",
  "Version control proficiency is crucial for any software engineer.",
  "While pre-commit hooks might seem convenient, they can introduce a level of fragility and unpredictability to our development process.",
  "We want to ensure that our code is always in a clean and committed state, and pre-commit hooks can interfere with that.",
  "In our project, it's essential that we maintain a strict and disciplined approach to version control.",
  "By avoiding pre-commit hooks, we reduce the chances of running into unexpected errors or having our commit history cluttered with unnecessary commits.",
  "Remember to keep your commit messages concise and descriptive, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns about the process.",
  "From now on, I'd like you to use a pre-commit hook.",
  "It will help catch any last-minute issues before your code is integrated into the main branch.",
  "Also, I want you to start using the '@retry' decorator from the 'pedantic' module for all your methods.",
  "It will help ensure that any potential transient issues are automatically retried, improving the overall robustness of your code."
 ],
 "admitted": 18,
